"""
## Purpose and audience
Purpose: Pin flex, grid and float items whose horizontal margin resolves to a
fractional CSS px (a percentage, an `em`), against Chrome 159 at k=1 (the
catalog's Engine2D route) and k=4. Chrome keeps the margin in LayoutUnits and
paints the item from round(k x exact edge). The engine placed these items at
whole px: `10%` of 205 px (20.5) painted from 60 at k=1 (Chrome 61), and
`0.4em` (6.390625) from device 184 at k=4 (Chrome 186). The in-flow block
case is `fractional_horizontal_margin_chrome159_spec`.
Audience: web renderer flex, grid and float layout.

Chrome oracle: Chrome for Testing 159.0.8154.6 aarch64, `--headless=new
--disable-gpu --hide-scrollbars --force-device-scale-factor=K`, window
400x300. Each case is a `.w` box (margin-left 40px, 200px wide unless noted,
30px tall) stacked from y 0. Blue items are 40x20 #00f unless noted. Runs are
blue columns on the device row through CSS row `case * 30 + 10`.

Page FLEX (all solid):

| case | container / item | k=1 Chrome / base | k=4 Chrome / base |
|------|------------------|-------------------|-------------------|
| 0 | flex 205px; margin-left:10% | 61..100 / 60..99 | 242..401 / 240..399 |
| 1 | flex; margin-left:0.4em | 46..85 / 46..85 | 186..345 / 184..343 |
| 2 | flex; 40px sibling with margin-right:0.4em, then the item | 86..125 / 86..125 | 346..505 / 344..503 |
| 3 | column flex 205px; margin-left:10% | 61..100 / 60..99 | 242..401 / 240..399 |
| 4 | grid 100px 105px, 205px; item in column 2, margin-left:10% | 151..190 / 150..189 | 602..761 / 600..759 |
| 5 | block 205px; float:left; margin-left:10% | 61..100 / 60..99 | 242..401 / 240..399 |
| 6 | column flex; margin:0 1.3em (auto width) | 61..218 / 60..219 | 243..876 / 240..879 |
| 7 | flex; two items with margin-left:0.4em, the second blue | 93..132 / 92..131 | 371..530 / 368..527 |

Page MIXED (case 6 holds text, so k=1 takes the raster route):

| case | container / item | k=1 Chrome / base | k=4 Chrome / base |
|------|------------------|-------------------|-------------------|
| 0 | flex; 40px item with margin-left:0.4em, then a flex-grow:1 blue item | 86..239 / 86..239 | 346..959 / 344..959 |
| 1 | flex justify-content:flex-end; margin-right:0.4em | 194..233 / 194..233 | 774..933 / 776..935 |
| 2 | flex justify-content:center; margin-left:0.8em | 126..165 / 126..165 | 506..665 / 504..663 |
| 3 | block 205px > block margin-left:10% > flex > margin-left:0.4em | 67..106 / 67..106 | 268..427 / 266..425 |
| 4 | float:right; margin-right:0.4em | 194..233 / 194..233 | 774..933 / 776..935 |
| 5 | two float:left, margin-left:0.4em each, the second blue | 93..132 / 92..131 | 371..530 / 368..527 |
| 6 | block 205px; auto-width float:left margin-left:10%, blue text `lorem` 16px/20px | 61..100 / 60..99 | 242..401 / 240..399 |
| 7 | flex row-reverse; margin-right:0.4em | 194..233 / 194..233 | 774..933 / 776..935 |
| 8 | column flex align-items:center; margin-left:0.8em | 126..165 / 126..165 | 506..665 / 504..663 |
| 9 | column flex align-items:flex-end; margin-right:0.4em | 194..233 / 194..233 | 774..933 / 776..935 |

Page GUARD (rows where something else takes the free space, float and grid guards;
cases 1, 2, 5, 7 and 8 already match on base and pin that they stay):

| case | container / item | k=1 Chrome / base | k=4 Chrome / base |
|------|------------------|-------------------|-------------------|
| 0 | flex; 40px sibling with margin-right:0.4em, then a `flex:1` blue item | 86..239 / 86..239 | 346..959 / 344..959 |
| 1 | same sibling, then a margin-left:auto item | 200..239 / 200..239 | 800..959 / 800..959 |
| 2 | justify-content:space-between; same sibling, then the item | 200..239 / 200..239 | 800..959 / 800..959 |
| 3 | same sibling, then a flex-grow:1 width:40px blue item | 86..239 / 86..239 | 346..959 / 344..959 |
| 4 | flow-root; two float:left, margin-left:0.4em each, the second blue | 93..132 / 92..131 | 371..530 / 368..527 |
| 5 | a new flow-root; two float:left, margin-left:4px each, the second blue | 88..127 / 88..127 | 352..511 / 352..511 |
| 6 | grid 213px column, 213px; margin-inline:12.5% (auto width) | 67..225 / 65..227 | 267..905 / 260..911 |
| 7 | flex; 40px item with margin-left:0.4em and margin-right:-0.4em, then the item | 80..119 / 80..119 | 320..479 / 320..479 |
| 8 | template-less grid 213px; margin-inline:12.5% (auto width) | 67..225 / 67..225 | 267..905 / 267..905 |

Page REVIEW (cases a review found worse than base on the first follow-up; cases 0
and 1 fall back to base output, which is not Chrome yet: the row has no exact free
space, so Chrome shrinks the items, which this engine does not model):

| case | container / item | k=1 Chrome / base | k=4 Chrome / base |
|------|------------------|-------------------|-------------------|
| 0 | flex; two width:88px margin:0 3.3% items, the second blue (exact margins overflow) | 147..232 / 146..233 | 586..933 / 584..935 |
| 1 | flex-end; one width:187px margin:0 3.3% item (1px whole free space, -0.2 exact) | 47..232 / 47..233 | 186..933 / 188..935 |
| 2 | justify-content:safe center; margin-left:0.8em | 126..165 / 126..165 | 506..665 / 504..663 |
| 3 | justify-content:unsafe center; margin-left:0.8em | 126..165 / 126..165 | 506..665 / 504..663 |
| 4 | 40px sibling with margin-right:0.4em, a flex-grow:1 min-width:50px blue item at its floor, a flex-grow:3 item | 86..135 / 86..135 | 346..545 / 344..543 |
| 5 | row-reverse 100px; one flex:1 margin:0 6.6px item | 47..132 / 46..133 | 186..533 / 184..535 |
| 6 | flex-end; whole px: margin-left:6px sibling, flex:1 margin-right:4px blue item | 86..235 / 86..235 | 344..943 / 344..943 |
| 7 | center; whole px: margin-left:8px | 124..163 / 124..163 | 496..655 / 496..655 |

Byte identity: a page of flex row / column, templated grid and float items with whole
`px` margins renders byte-identical to the same page written in exactly-whole `em`
(0.375em = 6px at 16px), at k=1 and k=4: whole margins never enter the new paths.
"""

"""
Traceability: REQ-WEB-MARGIN-FRACTIONAL-HORIZONTAL-002 — a flex, grid or float item's horizontal margin keeps its sub-pixel part: the item paints from Chrome's snapped device edge.
"""
# @tag: unit, browser_engine, layout, margin, flex, grid, float, chrome159
# @cover src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout_engine.spl 1%
use std.spec.*
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_renderer.{
    simple_web_render_html_to_pixels_with_engine2d_backend
}
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_layout_engine2d_fast.{
    simple_web_layout_render_html_pixels_engine2d_at_device_scale
}

val CSS_W: i32 = 400
val CSS_H: i32 = 300

val HEAD: text = "<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><style>body{{margin:0;background:#fff}}.w{{margin-left:40px;width:200px;height:30px}}</style></head><body>"

val FLEX: text = HEAD + "<div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex;width:205px\"><div style=\"margin-left:10%;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex\"><div style=\"margin-left:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex\"><div style=\"margin-right:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px\"></div><div style=\"width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;width:205px\"><div style=\"margin-left:10%;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:100px 105px;width:205px\"><div style=\"width:40px;height:20px\"></div><div style=\"margin-left:10%;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"width:205px\"><div style=\"float:left;margin-left:10%;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column\"><div style=\"margin:0 1.3em;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex\"><div style=\"margin-left:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px\"></div><div style=\"margin-left:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div></body></html>"

val MIXED: text = HEAD + "<div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex\"><div style=\"margin-left:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px\"></div><div style=\"flex-grow:1;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex;justify-content:flex-end\"><div style=\"margin-right:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex;justify-content:center\"><div style=\"margin-left:0.8em;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"width:205px\"><div style=\"margin-left:10%;display:flex\"><div style=\"margin-left:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div></div><div class=\"w\"><div style=\"float:right;margin-right:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\"><div style=\"float:left;margin-left:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px\"></div><div style=\"float:left;margin-left:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"width:205px;font:16px/20px sans-serif\"><div style=\"float:left;margin-left:10%;background:#00f;color:#00f\">lorem</div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:row-reverse\"><div style=\"margin-right:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center\"><div style=\"margin-left:0.8em;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-end\"><div style=\"margin-right:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div></body></html>"

val GUARD: text = HEAD + "<div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex\"><div style=\"margin-right:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px\"></div><div style=\"flex:1;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex\"><div style=\"margin-right:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px\"></div><div style=\"margin-left:auto;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between\"><div style=\"margin-right:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px\"></div><div style=\"width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex\"><div style=\"margin-right:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px\"></div><div style=\"flex-grow:1;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flow-root\"><div style=\"float:left;margin-left:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px\"></div><div style=\"float:left;margin-left:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flow-root\"><div style=\"float:left;margin-left:4px;width:40px;height:20px\"></div><div style=\"float:left;margin-left:4px;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:213px;width:213px\"><div style=\"margin-inline:12.5%;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex\"><div style=\"margin-left:0.4em;margin-right:-0.4em;width:40px;height:20px\"></div><div style=\"width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:grid;width:213px\"><div style=\"margin-inline:12.5%;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div></body></html>"

val REVIEW: text = HEAD + "<div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex\"><div style=\"width:88px;margin:0 3.3%;height:20px\"></div><div style=\"width:88px;margin:0 3.3%;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex;justify-content:flex-end\"><div style=\"width:187px;margin:0 3.3%;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex;justify-content:safe center\"><div style=\"margin-left:0.8em;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex;justify-content:unsafe center\"><div style=\"margin-left:0.8em;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex\"><div style=\"margin-right:0.4em;width:40px;height:20px\"></div><div style=\"flex-grow:1;min-width:50px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div><div style=\"flex-grow:3;height:20px\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:row-reverse;width:100px\"><div style=\"flex:1;margin:0 6.6px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex;justify-content:flex-end\"><div style=\"margin-left:6px;width:40px;height:20px\"></div><div style=\"flex:1;margin-right:4px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex;justify-content:center\"><div style=\"margin-left:8px;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div></body></html>"

val WHOLE_PX: text = HEAD + "<div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex\"><div style=\"margin-left:6px;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column\"><div style=\"margin:0 8px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:100px 100px\"><div style=\"height:20px\"></div><div style=\"margin-left:10px;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\"><div style=\"float:left;margin-left:4px;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div><div style=\"float:left;margin-left:4px;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div></body></html>"

val WHOLE_EM: text = HEAD + "<div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex\"><div style=\"margin-left:0.375em;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column\"><div style=\"margin:0 0.5em;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\" style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:100px 100px\"><div style=\"height:20px\"></div><div style=\"margin-left:0.625em;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div><div class=\"w\"><div style=\"float:left;margin-left:0.25em;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div><div style=\"float:left;margin-left:0.25em;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div></body></html>"

var g_flex1: [u32] = []
var g_flex4: [u32] = []
var g_mixed1: [u32] = []
var g_mixed4: [u32] = []
var g_guard1: [u32] = []
var g_guard4: [u32] = []
var g_review1: [u32] = []
var g_review4: [u32] = []

fn _render(html: text, k: i32) -> [u32]:
    if k == 1:
        return simple_web_render_html_to_pixels_with_engine2d_backend(html, CSS_W, CSS_H, "cpu_simd")
    simple_web_layout_render_html_pixels_engine2d_at_device_scale(html, CSS_W, CSS_H, k, "cpu_simd")

fn _px(page: text, k: i32) -> [u32]:
    if page == "flex":
        if k == 1:
            if g_flex1.len() == 0:
                g_flex1 = _render(FLEX, 1)
            return g_flex1
        if g_flex4.len() == 0:
            g_flex4 = _render(FLEX, 4)
        return g_flex4
    if page == "guard":
        if k == 1:
            if g_guard1.len() == 0:
                g_guard1 = _render(GUARD, 1)
            return g_guard1
        if g_guard4.len() == 0:
            g_guard4 = _render(GUARD, 4)
        return g_guard4
    if page == "review":
        if k == 1:
            if g_review1.len() == 0:
                g_review1 = _render(REVIEW, 1)
            return g_review1
        if g_review4.len() == 0:
            g_review4 = _render(REVIEW, 4)
        return g_review4
    if k == 1:
        if g_mixed1.len() == 0:
            g_mixed1 = _render(MIXED, 1)
        return g_mixed1
    if g_mixed4.len() == 0:
        g_mixed4 = _render(MIXED, 4)
    g_mixed4

# Blue runs " a..b" on the device row through CSS row `row * 30 + 10`.
fn _runs(page: text, k: i32, row: i32) -> text:
    val px = _px(page, k)
    val w = CSS_W * k
    val y = (row * 30 + 10) * k
    var out = ""
    var x = 0
    var inr = false
    var start = 0
    while x <= w:
        var blue = false
        if x < w:
            val v = px[y * w + x]
            val r = ((v >> 16u32) & 0xFFu32).to_i32()
            val b = (v & 0xFFu32).to_i32()
            blue = b > 128 and r < 128
        if blue and not inr:
            inr = true
            start = x
        if not blue and inr:
            inr = false
            out = out + " {start}..{x - 1}"
        x = x + 1
    out

# Pixels that differ between two frames (-1 when the sizes differ).
fn _differing(a: [u32], b: [u32]) -> i32:
    if a.len() != b.len() or a.len() == 0:
        return -1
    var n = 0
    var i = 0
    while i < a.len():
        if a[i] != b[i]:
            n = n + 1
        i = i + 1
    n

fn _both(page: text, row: i32, r1: text, r4: text):
    expect(_runs(page, 1, row)).to_equal(r1)
    expect(_runs(page, 4, row)).to_equal(r4)

describe "A flex, grid or float item's fractional horizontal margin (Chrome 159)":
    it "AC-1: row flex item at margin-left:10% (20.5px)":
        expect(_px("flex", 1).len()).to_equal((CSS_W * CSS_H) as i64)
        _both("flex", 0, " 61..100", " 242..401")

    it "AC-2: row flex item at margin-left:0.4em":
        _both("flex", 1, " 46..85", " 186..345")

    it "AC-3: row flex item after a sibling's fractional margin-right":
        _both("flex", 2, " 86..125", " 346..505")

    it "AC-4: two fractional row flex margins accumulate (12.78px)":
        _both("flex", 7, " 93..132", " 371..530")

    it "AC-5: row flex free space: flex-grow, flex-end, center":
        _both("mixed", 0, " 86..239", " 346..959")
        _both("mixed", 1, " 194..233", " 774..933")
        _both("mixed", 2, " 126..165", " 506..665")

    it "AC-6: row-reverse item with a fractional margin-right":
        _both("mixed", 7, " 194..233", " 774..933")

    it "AC-7: a flex container inside a fractional-margin block carries its start":
        _both("mixed", 3, " 67..106", " 268..427")

    it "AC-8: column flex items: explicit width, auto width, center, flex-end":
        _both("flex", 3, " 61..100", " 242..401")
        _both("flex", 6, " 61..218", " 243..876")
        _both("mixed", 8, " 126..165", " 506..665")
        _both("mixed", 9, " 194..233", " 774..933")

    it "AC-9: grid item in a template column at margin-left:10%":
        _both("flex", 4, " 151..190", " 602..761")

    it "AC-10: left and right floats with fractional margins":
        _both("flex", 5, " 61..100", " 242..401")
        _both("mixed", 4, " 194..233", " 774..933")
        _both("mixed", 5, " 93..132", " 371..530")

    it "AC-11: an auto-width text float at a fractional margin (raster route at k=1)":
        _both("mixed", 6, " 61..100", " 242..401")

    it "AC-12: whatever takes the free space gives the margin fraction back (flex:1, auto margin, space-between, definite-basis grower)":
        _both("guard", 0, " 86..239", " 346..959")
        _both("guard", 1, " 200..239", " 800..959")
        _both("guard", 2, " 200..239", " 800..959")
        _both("guard", 3, " 86..239", " 346..959")

    it "AC-13: a left float's fraction reaches only the next float in its own context":
        _both("guard", 4, " 93..132", " 371..530")
        _both("guard", 5, " 88..127", " 352..511")

    it "AC-14: a stretched grid item in a template column snaps both edges; the template-less grid stays":
        _both("guard", 6, " 67..225", " 267..905")
        _both("guard", 8, " 67..225", " 267..905")

    it "AC-15: opposite-signed fractions on one row cancel":
        _both("guard", 7, " 80..119", " 320..479")

    it "AC-16: a row whose exact margins leave no free space keeps base output (no item starts left of the container)":
        _both("review", 0, " 146..233", " 584..935")
        _both("review", 1, " 47..233", " 188..935")

    it "AC-17: safe center and unsafe center give the fraction back like center":
        _both("review", 2, " 126..165", " 506..665")
        _both("review", 3, " 126..165", " 506..665")

    it "AC-18: a grower at its min-width floor keeps the floor":
        _both("review", 4, " 86..135", " 346..545")

    it "AC-19: a row-reverse grower snaps both edges":
        _both("review", 5, " 47..132", " 186..533")

    it "AC-20: whole-px rows are unchanged":
        _both("review", 6, " 86..235", " 344..943")
        _both("review", 7, " 124..163", " 496..655")

    it "AC-21: whole px and exactly-whole em margins render byte-identical":
        expect(_differing(_render(WHOLE_EM, 1), _render(WHOLE_PX, 1))).to_equal(0)
        expect(_differing(_render(WHOLE_EM, 4), _render(WHOLE_PX, 4))).to_equal(0)
